^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[dcl.struct.bind]/4: when std::tuple_size<E> is a complete type with a member
`value`, a structured binding binds each name to get<i>(e) (typed
std::tuple_element<i, E>::type), not to the i-th data member.  CBMC now detects
std::tuple_size<E> and decomposes via get<i>(e); types without a tuple_size
specialization keep the data-member decomposition.  (std::tuple itself is not
yet detected -- its variadic tuple_size partial specialization does not resolve
in the probe -- but std::pair and other tuple-like types with a resolvable
tuple_size now decompose correctly.)

